# Python Commands via uv

- Use `uv` to execute all Python-related commands so tools run in the repo's local `.venv`.
- Do not run `python`, `pip`, `pytest`, or similar commands directly.

## Required command style

```bash
# Install / sync dependencies
uv sync

# Run Python scripts/modules
uv run python main.py
uv run python -m package.module

# Run tests
uv run pytest
uv run pytest -k "pattern"
```

## Avoid

```bash
python main.py
pytest
pip install -r requirements.txt
```
